@@ -0,0 +1,204 @@
+id: 2026-10-10-truthful-test-and-typecheck-gates
+title: Typecheck, lint and e2e gates that check what they claim
+priority: normal
+area: infra
+type: correctness
+delivery: code-patch
+intent: >
+  Make every project's typecheck cover all of its TypeScript and fail when it checks nothing, and
+  make lint reach every project.
+
+  Add scripts/typecheck-project.mjs and the local Nx plugin tools/nx-plugins/typecheck.js, and
+  list the plugin last in nx.json plugins so its `typecheck` target replaces the inferred
+  `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.lib.json`. The runner checks every config a project's tsconfig.json
+  references inside the project (lib/app, spec, storybook) one at a time with `tsc --noEmit`, and
+  fails when a config resolves no files, when an `exclude` inherited through `extends` removes files
+  the config's own `include` asks for, or when a tracked .ts/.tsx file under the project, build-tool
+  configs such as vite.config.ts included, is in no checked config. Only a nested directory with
+  both its own project.json and tsconfig.json (one the plugin gives a target) counts as a separate
+  project; either file alone does not hide its files. Projects whose
+  typecheck target is written in project.json (apps/api with tsconfig.typecheck.json, apps/web
+  after typegen) call the runner too, keeping their dependsOn. Typecheck inputs use `default`, not
+  `production`, so spec edits invalidate the cache.
+
+  Give every tsconfig.spec.json its own `exclude`. The workspace base config excludes
+  `**/*.spec.ts`, `**/*.test.ts` and their tsx forms, and a spec config that inherits that exclude
+  checks no spec at all. Add spec configs (and the solution-config reference) for libraries whose
+  specs had none, and include test folders outside src (for example apps/web/tests) in the spec
+  config that runs them. Then fix the type errors this exposes in tests, stories and tool configs
+  rather than excluding files or loosening strict.
+
+  Remove `@react-router/dev` and `@types/node` from apps/web/package.json devDependencies; the root
+  manifest declares both. The app-level copies resolved a second Vite with different peers, whose
+  Plugin type is nominally distinct from the root Vite's, so apps/web/vite.config.ts could not
+  typecheck.
+
+  Delete libs/api/core/data-access/src/lib/models/chapter-stats.ts and user-stats.ts. Nothing
+  imports them and no index exports them; they surfaced once libs/api code had its own typecheck.
+
+  Widen the web-ui social-links `member` prop from `Partial<User>` to `SocialLinkMember` (Partial<User>
+  plus the facebook/twitter/linkedin/instagram/youtube fields the component reads), and fix stories
+  that passed props their components do not have: the data-table `Loading` story becomes `Empty`,
+  and the simple-list-item stories become `NotClickable`/`Clickable` with the `Selected` story
+  removed.
+
+  Rename the inferred ESLint target from `eslint:lint` to `lint` in nx.json so `pnpm lint` and CI's
+  `nx affected -t lint` reach every project, and fix the lint errors that surfaces.
+
+  Make the API e2e result mean that the suite ran and passed. `api-e2e:e2e` runs the same wrapper as
+  `api-e2e:test` (apps/api-e2e/run-tests.sh) instead of the Vitest executor, and both targets set
+  `cache: false`. The wrapper reports PASSED only when Vitest exits 0, its summary counts no failure,
+  and at least one test passed, and prints that count; a run with no test file, or with every test
+  skipped, fails. Remove the wrapper's force-kill fallback, which accepted a non-zero exit when a
+  "Cleanup complete" marker appeared: teardown no longer calls process.exit and nothing prints the
+  marker. The e2e Vitest config sets `passWithNoTests: false` and the verbose reporter so the log
+  names every test, and drops both `dangerouslyIgnoreUnhandledErrors` and the onUnhandledError
+  filter for process.exit errors, so every unhandled error fails the run. Remove SKIP_API_CHECK and the
+  `__SKIP_E2E_TESTS__` flag: global setup set it on globalThis, which never reaches the forked test
+  worker, so the option produced a run of failures rather than a skip.
+
+  Resolve the test database URL in one place. apps/api-e2e/src/support/test-db.ts exports
+  testDatabaseUrl (TEST_DATABASE_URL, else `scripts/test-db.sh url`, the same answer the shell
+  runners use); global setup, test setup and specs import it instead of each carrying the template's
+  hard-coded fallback URL. Replace psql with the pg client: test-db.ts runs SQL through
+  apps/api-e2e/src/support/sql-runner.mjs, which keeps `sql()` synchronous and its `psql -At`
+  output (`|`-joined columns, server text values, one row per line, `:'name'` variables quoted as
+  literals, statements run one at a time with autocommit). Global setup's database probe and
+  disposable-database reset, and the wrapper's probe, use it too; the wrapper probe now uses the
+  URL's own credentials rather than postgres:postgres. Add @types/pg to devDependencies.
+
+  Stop the e2e API's whole process tree on native Windows. apps/api-e2e/src/support/api-process.ts
+  exports ownedProcessOptions(): POSIX keeps the detached process group; Windows keeps the launcher
+  attached and runs it through a shell, because pnpm is a .cmd shim that Node does not run without
+  one (global setup's `pnpm prisma migrate deploy` gets the same shell). killApiProcessTree runs
+  `%SystemRoot%\System32\taskkill.exe /PID <launcher> /T /F` on Windows and returns `tree`, treats
+  taskkill's not-found status (128) as already stopped, never runs it for a launcher Node has
+  already reaped, and throws on any other status, so teardown fails and the exit fallback retries.
+  Teardown logs the tree it stopped. Add process-tree-fixture.mjs and api-process.native.spec.ts,
+  which start a real launcher and descendant and check both stop on teardown, on SIGINT/SIGTERM
+  cancellation and from the exit fallback, plus (on Windows) that a taskkill failure is reported;
+  run them in test-support and in a windows-latest CI job.
+why: >
+  Spec files were never typechecked in any project: each spec config inherited the base
+  `**/*.spec.ts` exclude, so `tsc -p tsconfig.spec.json` compiled only a vite config or nothing.
+  `api-e2e:typecheck` ran `tsc -p` on a solution config with `files: []` and `include: []`, which
+  compiles zero files and exits 0. Libraries without a Vite or React Router plugin target (every
+  libs/api library) had no typecheck at all, so code only they contained was never checked, and
+  `pnpm lint`/CI lint ran ESLint for one project because the others' target was named
+  `eslint:lint`. Each of these reported green without checking the code. Enabling the checks found
+  real defects, including an e2e port wait passing an option the helper ignores.
+
+  The e2e gate had the same shape. `api-e2e:e2e` inherited `cache: true` and `passWithNoTests: true`
+  from the Vitest target defaults, so a green result could be a replay or a run of nothing, and
+  through Nx the log showed only a summary. `dangerouslyIgnoreUnhandledErrors` let any unhandled
+  error pass. The wrapper's probe used fixed postgres:postgres credentials: against CI's prisma
+  login it always failed and started a container the tests never used. test-db.ts needed a psql
+  binary that not every machine has, and three files hard-coded the template's own test URL, so a
+  clone on another port block reached the wrong database when run outside the wrappers.
+
+  On native Windows, teardown and cancellation killed only the pnpm launcher; the Nx and API
+  processes it started survived and kept the e2e port, so the next run attached to, or failed
+  against, a stale API. Setup could not start the API there at all: spawning `pnpm` without a shell
+  fails on Windows.
+affectedPaths:
