+  - AGENTS.md
+verification:
+  - node --test scripts/typecheck-project.spec.mjs
+  - pnpm exec nx run-many -t typecheck --skip-nx-cache
+  - pnpm exec nx run-many -t lint
+  - pnpm test
+  - pnpm exec nx run api-e2e:test-support --skip-nx-cache
+  - pnpm exec nx run api-e2e:e2e
+agentHints:
+  - >
+    Expect the first run to fail with real errors in specs, stories and tool configs that were
+    never checked. Fix them in the tests and configs; change product source only where the error
+    shows the product type is wrong. Do not add @ts-ignore, broad any casts, or excludes to get green.
+  - >
+    Downstream libraries are covered automatically once the plugin is registered; any project the
+    runner reports with an uncovered file needs that file added to the config that matches how it
+    runs (lib/app, spec or storybook), or a spec config created and referenced from tsconfig.json.
+  - >
+    If CI, scripts or docs call `eslint:lint`, rename them to `lint`. A project.json `lint` target
+    still overrides the inferred one.
+  - >
+    Typecheck now runs spec configs as well, so it does more work; configs run one at a time per
+    project. If `nx run-many -t typecheck` runs out of memory on a small machine or CI runner, run it
+    with `--parallel=1`. A lower-memory typecheck follows in a later release.
+  - >
+    Vitest 4 no longer adds `test` to Vite's config type: a vitest.config that imports defineConfig
+    from 'vite' fails typecheck. Import defineConfig from 'vitest/config'. Storybook 10 packages
+    resolve only through package exports, so storybook and spec configs that load them need
+    moduleResolution bundler.
+  - >
+    If apps/web/vite.config.ts fails with two incompatible Vite Plugin types, apps/web still declares
+    its own @react-router/dev or @types/node. Remove them (keep the root versions), run pnpm install,
+    and confirm `ls node_modules/.pnpm | grep '^vite@'` shows one entry. Do not bridge it with a cast.
+  - >
+    Build-tool configs (vite.config.ts, vitest.config.mts, jest.config.ts) must sit in a checked
+    config too, normally the spec config. An unused one can be deleted instead.
+  - >
+    Template promotion and patch apply never delete files, so remove the two stats model files by
+    hand. First search the project for imports of ChapterStats or UserStats (or the file names): if
+    the project uses them, keep the files, add them to a checked config, and record the deletion as
+    not-applicable. A project with its own stories may have more stale args; fix them the same way.
+  - >
+    Specs that call psql or the pg client themselves, or that read TEST_DATABASE_URL with their own
+    fallback, should import sql and testDatabaseUrl from support/test-db instead. If a spec relied on
+    psql printing command tags (`UPDATE 1`), the pg runner prints rows only; take the rows you need.
+  - >
+    If CI or scripts set SKIP_API_CHECK=true, it never skipped anything; remove it. To skip e2e, do
+    not run the target. If CI calls `nx e2e api-e2e` and a workspace targetDefaults entry caches it,
+    the project.json `cache: false` now overrides it.
+  - >
+    A project whose wrapper differs from the template's must still refuse PASSED when the Vitest
+    summary counts any failure (this fix is in the template since 2026-10-05) or no passed test.
+  - >
+    If the project changed how global setup starts the API, keep its spawn options from
+    ownedProcessOptions() (or the same detached/shell split) so teardown can reach every descendant.
+    A project without Windows developers or CI can leave out the windows-latest job, but keep the
+    native spec in test-support: on Linux and macOS it checks the process-group path.
